  abstract = {Musicare DB – A Database of Incomplete Printed Music is a scholarly resource cataloguing music prints with a focus on their state of preservation. The current scope covers Italian editions of sacred music (1580–1650), secular music (1580–1630), spiritual vernacular music (e.g. spiritual madrigals, 1580–1630), and instrumental music (1580–1640). Editions for which a complete set of partbooks survives in at least one copy are classified as complete; editions that, considering all known exemplars, have come down to us lacking one or more partbooks, or with one or more damaged partbooks, are classified as incomplete; incomplete editions for which a later issue exists that allows the set of partbooks to be completed are classified as completable. The census is based on a systematic survey of the following musicological resources, each referenced within the relevant entries: Répertoire International des Sources Musicales (RISM) A/I and B/I; RISM Online; the Printed Sacred Music Database; A Catalogue of Motets, Mass, Office, and Holy Week Music Printed in Italy, 1516–1770 (Kurtzman, Schnoebelen); Bibliografia della musica italiana vocale profana pubblicata dal 1500 al 1700 (Vogel, Einstein, Lesure, Sartori); RePIM – Repertorio della Poesia Italiana in Musica, 1500–1700 (Pompilio, Bonora); and Bibliografia della musica strumentale italiana stampata in Italia fino al 1700 (Sartori). This was supplemented with information from additional bibliographic sources and direct examination of the exemplars. This deposit contains a self-contained, browsable static HTML snapshot of the database (version 0.1.0), including all public catalogue pages, statistics, and search facilities; it can be opened directly from the archive without a server or internet connection. A later release will add the underlying relational data as CSV tables with an accompanying data dictionary. The continuously updated, live version of the database is served through the University of Padua's website at musicare.beniculturali.unipd.it/database/; this Zenodo deposit provides a permanent, citable snapshot of a specific state of that resource. Musicare DB is compiled and edited by Gabriele Taschetti, with data contribution by Chiara Comparin (instrumental music, 1580–1640), Enrico Scavo (secular and spiritual vernacular music, 1580–1630) and Gabriele Taschetti (sacred music, 1580–1650), within the project "MUSICARE – Musiche Incomplete: Censimento, Analisi, Restituzione / Taking CARE of Incomplete MUSIC" (scientific direction Marina Toffetti), University of Padua. How to Cite Gabriele Taschetti (ed.),~Musicare DB – A Database of Incomplete Printed Music, with data contribution by Chiara Comparin, Enrico Scavo and Gabriele Taschetti, project "MUSICARE – Musiche Incomplete: Censimento, Analisi, Restituzione / Taking CARE of Incomplete MUSIC" (scientific direction Marina Toffetti), University of Padua. Published 2026 [online]. DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.21234768.},
  langid = {english},
  version = {0.1.0},
  keywords = {16th centuty music,17th century music,early modern printed music,historical musicology,instrumental music,Italy,music bibliography,Musicology,partbooks,RISM,sacred music,secular music,source studies}
